#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133926 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133486 :question/id #uuid "4f12e12d-37b3-5c41-9284-bc369ccd4c0f" :question/math-academy-id "e-12421" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $\\Gamma$ of the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y,z) = y \\,\\mathbf{i} -x \\,\\mathbf{j} + z\\,\\mathbf{k}$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $\\mathbf r(t) =  \\sin (\\pi t)\\,\\mathbf{i} + \\cos (\\pi t)\\, \\mathbf{j} + t(2-t)\\,\\mathbf{k}$ for $t \\in [0,2].$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $\\Gamma$ measures the total work done by a force $\\mathbf F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\Gamma = \\oint\\limits_C \\mathbf F \\cdot \\textrm{d} \\mathbf r\n= \\int_a^b \\mathbf F(r(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf r'(t) \\; \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx = \\sin (\\pi t), \\qquad\ny = \\cos (\\pi t), \\qquad\nz = t(2-t) = 2t-t^2.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =y\\,i-x\\,j+z\\,k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j+(2t-{t}^{2})\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf r'(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t))\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t))\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-{t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,i-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j+2(1-t)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j+(2t-{t}^{2})\\,k\\,)\\cdot (\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,i-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j+2(1-t)\\,k) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\cdot \\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t))\\cdot (-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t))+(2t-{t}^{2})\\cdot 2(1-t) \\\\  & =\\pi {cos}^{2}⁡(\\pi t)+\\pi {sin}^{2}⁡(\\pi t)+2(2t-{t}^{2})(1-t) \\\\  & =\\pi ({cos}^{2}⁡(\\pi t)+{sin}^{2}⁡(\\pi t))+2(2t-3{t}^{2}+{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\pi +4t-6{t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\pi +4t-6{t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[\\pi t+2{t}^{2}-2{t}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{4}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =[2\\pi +8-16+8]-[0] \\\\  & =2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74196b81-0e52-5d10-a099-ccd849d03a98" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050773}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554914 :question-generator/id #uuid "c3c4b7ba-f69a-55fc-8713-34995bc1ce9b" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186133926.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134129 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f135681-35a3-57d6-b400-22964cf554ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279148} {:answer/id #uuid "3f1a53d4-a81b-5701-8651-a106eb9967eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279149} {:answer/id #uuid "494799ab-eb22-5d77-8cb0-046c691cba3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279245} {:answer/id #uuid "5aa0d2e3-2989-5892-b7f3-ebba5dfcf3d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279428} {:answer/id #uuid "d0ee7f1e-c3cb-5620-b310-57d2b69f3133" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f135681-35a3-57d6-b400-22964cf554ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279148} :answer-field/id #uuid "f075172d-b32a-5456-a8d7-c4de03227a4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281258}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "73fef5f2-e793-56dc-a75a-943258eb19b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-161925" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=y\\,i-x\\,j$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j+(1-{t}^{2})\\,k$ for $t\\in [-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t),\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t),\\,z=1-{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =y\\,i-x\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t))\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t))\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,i+\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j-2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j)\\cdot (-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,i+\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j-2t\\,k) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\cdot (-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t))+(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t))\\cdot \\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)+0\\cdot (-2t) \\\\  & =-\\pi {sin}^{2}⁡(\\pi t)-\\pi {cos}^{2}⁡(\\pi t) \\\\  & =-\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(-\\pi )\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\pi [t]_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\pi (1-(-1)) \\\\  & =-2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134133 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91e141a3-db78-5e44-a461-551fe7a0bece" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{60}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130955} {:answer/id #uuid "ad54536a-b558-5c60-b187-fd8fa41d6e02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130956} {:answer/id #uuid "e0ca6443-99c2-586e-b058-eaae89edfbc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130957} {:answer/id #uuid "2e445657-7a49-56a3-a596-aad6a22d87db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{100}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130958} {:answer/id #uuid "5e35f75a-b843-5afb-af33-d8260e24ea04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130959}] :answer-field/id #uuid "3d428aec-71bd-5e76-8cd2-9b96389f1f6c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130954}] :question/id #uuid "4bba2c4b-bfab-581e-aa67-d4d398fc018f" :question/math-academy-id "q-162238" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x, y, z) = (y - x)i$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t) = (t^{2} - t)i + (t^{3} - t)j + \\sin (2πt)k$ for $t ∈ [0, 1)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281416 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c03a648-3276-51bd-9904-df1d4522549b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278709} {:answer/id #uuid "0d190dfe-46ce-5dc3-b82b-670060383d50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278713} {:answer/id #uuid "2f78edf6-ba63-5eb2-ac9e-cec1baa76b5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279006} {:answer/id #uuid "7e9d76f8-5364-55b7-bd19-13182f53be56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279732} {:answer/id #uuid "dacdb6c9-01bb-5071-9c74-09822a99f555" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280523}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d190dfe-46ce-5dc3-b82b-670060383d50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278713} :answer-field/id #uuid "565bb2c5-d8e2-5a10-ab5d-91f31338f51b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280978}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c14a191e-1e95-5ff6-80a2-30d79cf0bf66" :question/math-academy-id "q-162220" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=y\\,i+x\\,j$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,z=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =y\\,i+x\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j)\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+0\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}{2}]_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281421 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2699a966-6b46-57cf-a47c-22a3c667651c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278937} {:answer/id #uuid "32391712-510d-5554-9a81-b26d6930e9b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279032} {:answer/id #uuid "7bcd3745-9952-55fa-8d98-6a218c3df910" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279695} {:answer/id #uuid "d4655d09-3913-5973-b875-0e396a2fcd45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280464} {:answer/id #uuid "dcaa048d-a79a-598e-9189-af11a04e4488" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dcaa048d-a79a-598e-9189-af11a04e4488" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280540} :answer-field/id #uuid "d03b1767-6387-503d-af9b-02fb2cde0ee3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281199}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fd877a62-b477-55ef-9e5a-194da8c5c887" :question/math-academy-id "q-162230" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=y\\,i-x\\,j+z\\,k$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\,j+{t}^{2}\\,k$ for $t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t),\\,y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t),\\,z={t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =y\\,i-x\\,j+z\\,k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,j+{t}^{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,j+2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,j+{t}^{2}\\,k)\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,j+2t\\,k) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))+{t}^{2}\\cdot 2t \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡(\\pi t)+{sin}^{2}⁡(t)+2{t}^{3} \\\\  & =1+2{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(1+2{t}^{3})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[t+\\frac{{t}^{4}}{2}]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =((\\pi -(-\\pi ))+\\frac{{\\pi }^{4}-(-\\pi )^{4}}{2}) \\\\  & =2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281422 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40f453c1-1269-5d7b-a9f7-d8c20a89e598" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279168} {:answer/id #uuid "7c949669-3c80-5476-91b1-fc3b5d631b2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279704} {:answer/id #uuid "a6e227ef-2347-5b50-9e1d-289d72ee8083" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280068} {:answer/id #uuid "d01a006d-cf1e-5f29-84c5-eff90c285d83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280422} {:answer/id #uuid "d6aa8cae-8f41-5bb7-8dbc-0f01c9e8efb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6aa8cae-8f41-5bb7-8dbc-0f01c9e8efb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280487} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8079c5b-3e54-561a-bcb4-10bee6629161" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281245}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "13da6f40-f5bf-549b-a97f-20a44b83344f" :question/math-academy-id "q-162235" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=(x+y)\\,i-z\\,k$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=(1-{t}^{2})\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,k$ for $t\\in [-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=1-{t}^{2},\\,y={t}^{2},\\,z=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t).\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(x+y)\\,i-z\\,k \\\\  & =(1-{t}^{2}+{t}^{2})\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,k \\\\  & =i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t))\\,k \\\\  & =-2t\\,i+2t\\,j+\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,k)\\cdot (-2t\\,i+2t\\,j+\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,k) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-2t)+0\\cdot 2t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\cdot \\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t) \\\\  & =-2t+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(-2t+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi t))\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[-{t}^{2}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi t)}{4}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(-1-\\frac{1}{4})-(-1-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281424 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1107e5cc-b9e4-51b4-b110-09cc2b0cd618" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278747} {:answer/id #uuid "3ffec3d9-ca96-573b-8802-6b5844531fec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279155} {:answer/id #uuid "92a000d5-a346-5920-a484-8ed38558a27d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279894} {:answer/id #uuid "f0d0e41b-2046-5460-a0ac-9936085c2a9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280693} {:answer/id #uuid "f3b31ed2-8b79-55de-ae35-ed2256356bcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ffec3d9-ca96-573b-8802-6b5844531fec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279155} :answer-field/id #uuid "5895b727-7ab1-5288-96b4-772760ec6b05" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280984}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b7cf2656-c8b3-55d8-81c3-17aef82ea92a" :question/math-academy-id "q-162237" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=-z\\,j+y\\,k$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,z=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =-z\\,j+y\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k)\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k) \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & ={sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t. \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[t]_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431183 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11019ac0-2397-5082-8da2-e2cda61c67f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431149} {:answer/id #uuid "2ca8c25f-0afe-549b-bd9e-0579f77dfd35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431152} {:answer/id #uuid "617b3f2e-e124-52d6-b054-729c57763e06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431157} {:answer/id #uuid "8493f5bf-0293-5a89-b43a-eae5ba48387d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431159} {:answer/id #uuid "e69380fc-03e3-562e-97ec-2bf770b22d2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ca8c25f-0afe-549b-bd9e-0579f77dfd35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431152} :answer-field/id #uuid "e84d6437-9ec9-5b4b-a3b3-8f14a689f608" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431181}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1d416162-8b5b-53c3-aa15-9f678fcebfbf" :question/math-academy-id "q-162229" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=-y\\,i+x\\,j$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j+2\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,2).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t),\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t),\\,z=2.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =-y\\,i+x\\,j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t))\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t))\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)\\,k \\\\  & =-2\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,i+\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j+0\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j)\\cdot (-2\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,i+\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j+0\\,k) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\cdot (-2\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t))+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\cdot \\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)+0\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =2\\pi {sin}^{2}⁡(\\pi t)+2\\pi {cos}^{2}⁡(\\pi t) \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2\\pi \\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\pi [t]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\pi (2-0) \\\\  & =4\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431188 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58c1fd16-ca29-5709-a267-219424eaaabc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431156} {:answer/id #uuid "8c03109d-b971-53ee-a86a-7e35ed350bb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431160} {:answer/id #uuid "adea9c1e-27a3-5208-9dd6-795f2fa57e6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431165} {:answer/id #uuid "b705117a-dca8-5892-b76c-7de8a8a5594d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431169} {:answer/id #uuid "d1fa4475-9d5e-511a-8566-852d47df5af6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b705117a-dca8-5892-b76c-7de8a8a5594d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431169} :answer-field/id #uuid "42e70451-3a35-5ee4-bde4-603fef9a0a12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431178}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9f4551bd-d0a1-5978-99b9-17e8a12314a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-162228" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=z\\,j-y\\,k$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=({t}^{2}-t)\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi t)\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi t)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1)$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx={t}^{2}-t,\\,y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi t),\\,z=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi t).\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =z\\,j-y\\,k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi t)\\,j-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi t)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi t))\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi t))\\,k \\\\  & =(2t-1)\\,i-2\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi t)\\,j+2\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi t)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi t)\\,j-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi t)\\,k)\\cdot ((2t-1)\\,i-2\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi t)\\,j+2\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi t)\\,k) \\\\  & =0\\cdot (2t-1)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi t)\\cdot (-2\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi t))+(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi t))\\cdot 2\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi t) \\\\  & =-2\\pi {sin}^{2}⁡(2\\pi t)-2\\pi {cos}^{2}⁡(2\\pi t) \\\\  & =-2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-2\\pi )\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2\\pi [t]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-2\\pi (1-0) \\\\  & =-2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521464 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1348fc00-336c-53bb-be7c-916496ef5d88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520808} {:answer/id #uuid "55053be1-77fb-5c4b-806e-49e7c1fc512f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520958} {:answer/id #uuid "662c897b-ead7-5be2-af3c-4e8c4cf7d102" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520996} {:answer/id #uuid "b48883a2-477f-5af5-a0a1-a15c7ffa7d19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521168} {:answer/id #uuid "c81bffa8-6d28-5db1-a4e4-943e85fac37c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c81bffa8-6d28-5db1-a4e4-943e85fac37c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521211} :answer-field/id #uuid "81425c09-b875-5245-8a44-a234fc04ecfd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521387}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "19360ab0-63c4-5cd8-9a4a-b29910944cd3" :question/math-academy-id "q-162232" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=x\\,i-z\\,k$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=({t}^{2}-t)\\,i+({t}^{3}-{t}^{2})\\,j+k$ for $t\\in [0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx={t}^{2}-t,\\,y={t}^{3}-{t}^{2},\\,z=1.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =x\\,i-z\\,k \\\\  & =({t}^{2}-t)\\,i-1\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-{t}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)\\,k \\\\  & =(2t-1)\\,i+(3{t}^{2}-2t)\\,j+0\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(({t}^{2}-t)\\,i-\\,k)\\cdot ((2t-1)\\,i+(3{t}^{2}-2t)\\,j) \\\\  & =({t}^{2}-t)\\cdot (2t-1)+0\\cdot (3{t}^{2}-2t)+(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =({t}^{2}-t)(2t-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({t}^{2}-t)(2t-1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[\\frac{({t}^{2}-t)^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(0-0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554853 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b337fa7-bd8b-5c90-a0a9-70650e2fdcbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554860} {:answer/id #uuid "7d135ef6-116e-5934-84c1-11a47c59668f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554878} {:answer/id #uuid "836d5d14-56d9-58cb-9958-435971a6cb35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554881} {:answer/id #uuid "8cf45132-d649-533a-9603-ef7dfcb122bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554884} {:answer/id #uuid "ce656dd1-358f-523e-9af0-50c385c018ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554904}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8cf45132-d649-533a-9603-ef7dfcb122bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554884} :answer-field/id #uuid "46488809-31b0-5e06-a0e3-3b15d04132fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554866}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0de1e67b-08b0-590a-987d-98f0797e3256" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=\\left(x + y\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(- z\\right)\\,k$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\left(4 - 4 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\left(4 t^{2}\\right)\\,j+\\left(\\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=4 - 4 t^{2},\\quad y=4 t^{2},\\quad z=\\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\left(x + y\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(- z\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(4\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(- \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(4 - 4 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(4 t^{2}\\right)\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(\\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(- 8 t\\right)\\,i+\\left(8 t\\right)\\,j+\\left(\\pi \\cos{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(\\left(4\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(- \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\left(- 8 t\\right)\\,i+\\left(8 t\\right)\\,j+\\left(\\pi \\cos{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(4\\right)\\cdot\\left(- 8 t\\right)+\\left(0\\right)\\cdot\\left(8 t\\right)+\\left(- \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\pi \\cos{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(- 32 t\\right)+\\left(0\\right)+\\left(- \\pi \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ & =- 32 t - \\frac{\\pi \\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr & =\\int_{-1}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\int_{-1}^{1}\\left(- 32 t - \\frac{\\pi \\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\left[- 16 t^{2} + \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}}{4}\\right]_{-1}^{1} \\\\ & =[\\left(-16\\right)+\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)]-[\\left(-16\\right)+\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)] \\\\ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554863 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38d9f40b-294c-5d0d-b920-423d8a07b7b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554864} {:answer/id #uuid "59829333-e505-5da3-98f2-21a5554e8c75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554870} {:answer/id #uuid "9b006bad-ce48-5e7e-a06c-1c336b782ab7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554888} {:answer/id #uuid "c0dc3100-368a-5fe9-8467-27205633130c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554902} {:answer/id #uuid "ed445195-4fe7-541a-8a1e-6f2a605ae973" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed445195-4fe7-541a-8a1e-6f2a605ae973" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554910} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d5efd9d-3e69-5f74-9f3d-3ac7e3057828" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554852}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "348e1450-060b-511e-ab1c-9ac3626ec2eb" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=\\left(- 6 x + 5 y\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\left(5 t^{2} - 5 t\\right)\\,i+\\left(6 t^{3} - 6 t\\right)\\,j+\\left(\\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=5 t^{2} - 5 t,\\quad y=6 t^{3} - 6 t,\\quad z=\\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\left(- 6 x + 5 y\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(30 t^{3} - 30 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(5 t^{2} - 5 t\\right)\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(6 t^{3} - 6 t\\right)\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(\\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(10 t - 5\\right)\\,i+\\left(18 t^{2} - 6\\right)\\,j+\\left(2 \\pi \\cos{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(\\left(30 t^{3} - 30 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\left(10 t - 5\\right)\\,i+\\left(18 t^{2} - 6\\right)\\,j+\\left(2 \\pi \\cos{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(30 t^{3} - 30 t^{2}\\right)\\cdot\\left(10 t - 5\\right)+\\left(0\\right)\\cdot\\left(18 t^{2} - 6\\right)+\\left(0\\right)\\cdot\\left(2 \\pi \\cos{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(300 t^{4} - 450 t^{3} + 150 t^{2}\\right)+\\left(0\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(10 t - 5\\right) \\left(30 t^{3} - 30 t^{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr & =\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left(10 t - 5\\right) \\left(30 t^{3} - 30 t^{2}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\left[60 t^{5} - \\frac{225 t^{4}}{2} + 50 t^{3}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =[\\left(50\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{225}{2}\\right)+\\left(60\\right)]-[\\left(0\\right)+\\left(0\\right)+\\left(0\\right)] \\\\ & =- \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554865 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "114cd428-9ff5-5378-aaf6-79f85ced9209" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554854} {:answer/id #uuid "685f9e08-daff-5c3f-b9a5-c47f24d86c3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554873} {:answer/id #uuid "9e82d924-eb43-5d3a-931f-13fe24c0e9e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554889} {:answer/id #uuid "a5ebf419-c2bb-56d3-aef3-a83b86af5ec7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554893} {:answer/id #uuid "ba8d6487-1209-5a0b-84d1-1ff1578aaccd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554898}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "114cd428-9ff5-5378-aaf6-79f85ced9209" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554854} :answer-field/id #uuid "32b499d6-e35b-5df6-b9cc-4a94b51e5a0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554862}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4133c25f-bd85-507a-8e90-bf61f17f7c85" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=\\left(x + y\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(- z\\right)\\,k$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\left(3 - 3 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\left(3 t^{2}\\right)\\,j+\\left(4 \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=3 - 3 t^{2},\\quad y=3 t^{2},\\quad z=4 \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\left(x + y\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(- z\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(3\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(- 4 \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(3 - 3 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(3 t^{2}\\right)\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(4 \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(- 6 t\\right)\\,i+\\left(6 t\\right)\\,j+\\left(4 \\pi \\cos{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(\\left(3\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(- 4 \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\left(- 6 t\\right)\\,i+\\left(6 t\\right)\\,j+\\left(4 \\pi \\cos{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(3\\right)\\cdot\\left(- 6 t\\right)+\\left(0\\right)\\cdot\\left(6 t\\right)+\\left(- 4 \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\cdot\\left(4 \\pi \\cos{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(- 18 t\\right)+\\left(0\\right)+\\left(- 16 \\pi \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ & =- 18 t - 8 \\pi \\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr & =\\int_{-1}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\int_{-1}^{1}\\left(- 18 t - 8 \\pi \\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\left[- 9 t^{2} + 4 \\cos{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right]_{-1}^{1} \\\\ & =[\\left(-9\\right)+\\left(4\\right)]-[\\left(-9\\right)+\\left(4\\right)] \\\\ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554867 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5603107d-9563-57f2-ba74-697614f507d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554868} {:answer/id #uuid "691dd10a-c57a-5d20-99c1-541d1fc7c15b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554874} {:answer/id #uuid "9f75d586-ec9d-5bbd-9ed9-a2cb0af7b409" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 24 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554890} {:answer/id #uuid "bab50ed0-e1ba-597a-9fae-6f0bc3a2cefc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554899} {:answer/id #uuid "ee9ac4e6-bfaf-5b63-9e0a-7f43b911ffbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554911}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee9ac4e6-bfaf-5b63-9e0a-7f43b911ffbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554911} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c07df69-ac22-576f-bdf1-ec7b4560369b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554875}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "551d4d7b-a286-5922-9bb8-28fd2d1e93e0" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=\\left(y\\right)\\,i+\\left(x\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\left(4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,i+\\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,j+\\left(2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,2 \\pi).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\quad y=3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\quad z=2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\left(y\\right)\\,i+\\left(x\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,i+\\left(4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,i+\\left(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,j+\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(\\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,i+\\left(4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\left(4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,i+\\left(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,j+\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\cdot\\left(4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)+\\left(4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\cdot\\left(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)+\\left(0\\right)\\cdot\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(12 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)+\\left(- 12 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =12 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr & =\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}\\left(12 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\left[6 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{2 \\pi} \\\\ & =[\\left(0\\right)]-[\\left(0\\right)] \\\\ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554872 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18df830f-ab86-5425-9738-33adc7144a61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554857} {:answer/id #uuid "7d2f5870-6bef-5a74-bac7-cea2f02dad0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554879} {:answer/id #uuid "bbe93c39-19b8-5993-86a0-832c5694d298" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554900} {:answer/id #uuid "bf92e1c7-9d7c-59ca-9b8b-0d362f20d0bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554901} {:answer/id #uuid "eb3c9e86-4f1e-5d6f-beb8-32c3b7b03702" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb3c9e86-4f1e-5d6f-beb8-32c3b7b03702" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554909} :answer-field/id #uuid "86fe68d1-7c6d-53bc-9521-f981d69d8bbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554882}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "62239d5b-2148-5cb6-b90b-702d31af6174" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=\\left(x + y\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(- z\\right)\\,k$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\left(2 - 2 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\left(2 t^{2}\\right)\\,j+\\left(\\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=2 - 2 t^{2},\\quad y=2 t^{2},\\quad z=\\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\left(x + y\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(- z\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(2\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(- \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(2 - 2 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(2 t^{2}\\right)\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(\\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(- 4 t\\right)\\,i+\\left(4 t\\right)\\,j+\\left(\\pi \\cos{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(\\left(2\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(- \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\left(- 4 t\\right)\\,i+\\left(4 t\\right)\\,j+\\left(\\pi \\cos{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(2\\right)\\cdot\\left(- 4 t\\right)+\\left(0\\right)\\cdot\\left(4 t\\right)+\\left(- \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\pi \\cos{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(- 8 t\\right)+\\left(0\\right)+\\left(- \\pi \\sin{\\left(\\pi t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\pi t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ & =- 8 t - \\frac{\\pi \\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr & =\\int_{-1}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\int_{-1}^{1}\\left(- 8 t - \\frac{\\pi \\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\left[- 4 t^{2} + \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}}{4}\\right]_{-1}^{1} \\\\ & =[\\left(-4\\right)+\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)]-[\\left(-4\\right)+\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)] \\\\ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554886 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "808a5326-9dff-5a55-9b39-14e73a8ade5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554880} {:answer/id #uuid "8dd73a49-9462-58fe-968c-112a2c100806" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554885} {:answer/id #uuid "c200f38f-c26e-5cd4-85db-52babd0f8f33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554903} {:answer/id #uuid "dc8e63f4-ed19-59b5-bc80-7949ae059bd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554907} {:answer/id #uuid "e2c2bc78-875e-5056-8106-c17473d134ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8dd73a49-9462-58fe-968c-112a2c100806" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554885} :answer-field/id #uuid "2412e38f-65d0-568d-9f2c-e830bb205b72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554859}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "90b5c24e-2e35-52ad-ab63-078b662235e0" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=\\left(- 3 x + y\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\left(t^{2} - t\\right)\\,i+\\left(3 t^{3} - 3 t\\right)\\,j+\\left(\\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=t^{2} - t,\\quad y=3 t^{3} - 3 t,\\quad z=\\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\left(- 3 x + y\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(3 t^{3} - 3 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(t^{2} - t\\right)\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(3 t^{3} - 3 t\\right)\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(\\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(2 t - 1\\right)\\,i+\\left(9 t^{2} - 3\\right)\\,j+\\left(2 \\pi \\cos{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(\\left(3 t^{3} - 3 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\left(2 t - 1\\right)\\,i+\\left(9 t^{2} - 3\\right)\\,j+\\left(2 \\pi \\cos{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(3 t^{3} - 3 t^{2}\\right)\\cdot\\left(2 t - 1\\right)+\\left(0\\right)\\cdot\\left(9 t^{2} - 3\\right)+\\left(0\\right)\\cdot\\left(2 \\pi \\cos{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(6 t^{4} - 9 t^{3} + 3 t^{2}\\right)+\\left(0\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(2 t - 1\\right) \\left(3 t^{3} - 3 t^{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr & =\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left(2 t - 1\\right) \\left(3 t^{3} - 3 t^{2}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\left[\\frac{6 t^{5}}{5} - \\frac{9 t^{4}}{4} + t^{3}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =[\\left(1\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{9}{4}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{6}{5}\\right)]-[\\left(0\\right)+\\left(0\\right)+\\left(0\\right)] \\\\ & =- \\frac{1}{20}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554891 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ac91a83-8224-5d8e-ba27-2b72dc0e550e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554871} {:answer/id #uuid "a2f5d5e8-72bf-5eef-9f66-1115edcbf08b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554892} {:answer/id #uuid "aeb0051e-3f8b-5982-b846-e7ff7eee0bc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554895} {:answer/id #uuid "b6bebfde-1b88-5d80-a03c-526c15e8086b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554897} {:answer/id #uuid "d7cd44d3-fba0-5f5a-9f78-907e87a97980" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554906}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7cd44d3-fba0-5f5a-9f78-907e87a97980" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554906} :answer-field/id #uuid "9141a1c6-310d-56d7-be04-c32575e4f57b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554887}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a2d5b731-3e56-5fb7-954f-29cf21b28b60" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=\\left(- 5 x + 3 y\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\left(3 t^{2} - 3 t\\right)\\,i+\\left(5 t^{3} - 5 t\\right)\\,j+\\left(\\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=3 t^{2} - 3 t,\\quad y=5 t^{3} - 5 t,\\quad z=\\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\left(- 5 x + 3 y\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(15 t^{3} - 15 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(3 t^{2} - 3 t\\right)\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(5 t^{3} - 5 t\\right)\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(\\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(6 t - 3\\right)\\,i+\\left(15 t^{2} - 5\\right)\\,j+\\left(2 \\pi \\cos{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(\\left(15 t^{3} - 15 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\left(6 t - 3\\right)\\,i+\\left(15 t^{2} - 5\\right)\\,j+\\left(2 \\pi \\cos{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(15 t^{3} - 15 t^{2}\\right)\\cdot\\left(6 t - 3\\right)+\\left(0\\right)\\cdot\\left(15 t^{2} - 5\\right)+\\left(0\\right)\\cdot\\left(2 \\pi \\cos{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(90 t^{4} - 135 t^{3} + 45 t^{2}\\right)+\\left(0\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(6 t - 3\\right) \\left(15 t^{3} - 15 t^{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr & =\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left(6 t - 3\\right) \\left(15 t^{3} - 15 t^{2}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\left[18 t^{5} - \\frac{135 t^{4}}{4} + 15 t^{3}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =[\\left(15\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{135}{4}\\right)+\\left(18\\right)]-[\\left(0\\right)+\\left(0\\right)+\\left(0\\right)] \\\\ & =- \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554912 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18dd15e6-ceda-574e-ae06-3f078dde4884" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554856} {:answer/id #uuid "2d9fb833-3125-5919-b437-36a3f7f5f96f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554861} {:answer/id #uuid "8b7a795b-920f-50ae-a34a-1268cb9c84e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554883} {:answer/id #uuid "af7a1424-420b-530b-a8b3-d9679923d02b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554896} {:answer/id #uuid "d449a91f-5788-54f4-828f-d3441dced376" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18dd15e6-ceda-574e-ae06-3f078dde4884" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554856} :answer-field/id #uuid "16a69a5b-1a25-591c-a7b0-93d8b7f7c7fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554855}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f1bb72e1-4e4c-5956-a260-d2f9af2fd428" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=\\left(- x + 4 y\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\left(4 t^{2} - 4 t\\right)\\,i+\\left(t^{3} - t\\right)\\,j+\\left(\\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=4 t^{2} - 4 t,\\quad y=t^{3} - t,\\quad z=\\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\left(- x + 4 y\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(4 t^{3} - 4 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(4 t^{2} - 4 t\\right)\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(t^{3} - t\\right)\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(\\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(8 t - 4\\right)\\,i+\\left(3 t^{2} - 1\\right)\\,j+\\left(2 \\pi \\cos{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(\\left(4 t^{3} - 4 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\left(8 t - 4\\right)\\,i+\\left(3 t^{2} - 1\\right)\\,j+\\left(2 \\pi \\cos{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(4 t^{3} - 4 t^{2}\\right)\\cdot\\left(8 t - 4\\right)+\\left(0\\right)\\cdot\\left(3 t^{2} - 1\\right)+\\left(0\\right)\\cdot\\left(2 \\pi \\cos{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(32 t^{4} - 48 t^{3} + 16 t^{2}\\right)+\\left(0\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(8 t - 4\\right) \\left(4 t^{3} - 4 t^{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr & =\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left(8 t - 4\\right) \\left(4 t^{3} - 4 t^{2}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\left[\\frac{32 t^{5}}{5} - 12 t^{4} + \\frac{16 t^{3}}{3}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =[\\left(\\frac{16}{3}\\right)+\\left(-12\\right)+\\left(\\frac{32}{5}\\right)]-[\\left(0\\right)+\\left(0\\right)+\\left(0\\right)] \\\\ & =- \\frac{4}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554913 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0107db86-5f81-5e7a-90b1-ac80539a2cab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554851} {:answer/id #uuid "563b3666-11ab-5f91-bf53-b00d149971a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554869} {:answer/id #uuid "7923bbea-5fc9-561d-8f9d-cbea6a7cc519" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554876} {:answer/id #uuid "7ae5c9e7-b57e-591d-b22b-fd4a0ce7f189" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554877} {:answer/id #uuid "a7530702-2dc7-5b8f-a27e-09042f5ae35e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554894}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7923bbea-5fc9-561d-8f9d-cbea6a7cc519" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554876} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ec2ef2e-3a51-5ca5-b6b9-538fa415f571" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554858}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f20d86c9-5c94-54b3-af24-d220a2e7aeac" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=\\left(- 5 x + 6 y\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\left(6 t^{2} - 6 t\\right)\\,i+\\left(5 t^{3} - 5 t\\right)\\,j+\\left(\\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=6 t^{2} - 6 t,\\quad y=5 t^{3} - 5 t,\\quad z=\\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\left(- 5 x + 6 y\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(30 t^{3} - 30 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(6 t^{2} - 6 t\\right)\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(5 t^{3} - 5 t\\right)\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(\\sin{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k \\\\ & =\\left(12 t - 6\\right)\\,i+\\left(15 t^{2} - 5\\right)\\,j+\\left(2 \\pi \\cos{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(\\left(30 t^{3} - 30 t^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\left(0\\right)\\,j+\\left(0\\right)\\,k\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\left(12 t - 6\\right)\\,i+\\left(15 t^{2} - 5\\right)\\,j+\\left(2 \\pi \\cos{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right)\\,k\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(30 t^{3} - 30 t^{2}\\right)\\cdot\\left(12 t - 6\\right)+\\left(0\\right)\\cdot\\left(15 t^{2} - 5\\right)+\\left(0\\right)\\cdot\\left(2 \\pi \\cos{\\left(2 \\pi t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(360 t^{4} - 540 t^{3} + 180 t^{2}\\right)+\\left(0\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(12 t - 6\\right) \\left(30 t^{3} - 30 t^{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ=\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr & =\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left(12 t - 6\\right) \\left(30 t^{3} - 30 t^{2}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\left[72 t^{5} - 135 t^{4} + 60 t^{3}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =[\\left(60\\right)+\\left(-135\\right)+\\left(72\\right)]-[\\left(0\\right)+\\left(0\\right)+\\left(0\\right)] \\\\ & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Circulation Over Space Curves"}]}
